{
  "bridge_text": "那棵大树的树干在寒风中低声吟唱，仿佛在呼唤着莉娜，催促她去探索那未完的秘密。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜裹紧了红色的羊毛大衣，穿过那片被冻得硬邦邦的田野，终于走到了树下。树干深处传来的嗡嗡声比在家中听到的还要清晰，像是无数只小蜜蜂在低语。她深吸一口气，拨开垂下的枯枝，迈进了那个从未被大人们踏足的神秘树洞。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Perhaps the secret he hides beneath his vest explains his sharp words, yet Lina stands her ground as the humming continues to pull at her curiosity. She waits to see if the fox will let her pass.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes meeting the fox’s gaze. She knew the humming was a mystery meant only for her to solve. Mosk flicked his tail, his whiskers twitching with a mix of annoyance and something softer, like a memory he tried to push away."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a clawed finger at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and whispered that it was for the trouble of walking her down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his expression unreadable. Then he stood up, pulled his vest tight, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Mosk twitched his ears, his green vest rustling as he watched Lina with those sharp, ancient eyes. Since the path forward is blocked by his stubbornness, let us see if an offering can change his mind.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a claw toward the door, but Lina reached into her pocket. She pulled out the very last apple of the season, setting it gently on the wooden step between them. She told him it was for the trouble of her visit, and for the long walk down. The fox stared at the red fruit for a long, heavy moment. Finally, he stood up, straightened his patched vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a single word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the winding stairs, the humming grew into a soft, melodic song. There lay a firefly the size of a robin, resting upon a bed of damp moss, her golden glow flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked down at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend, but one winter long ago, he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. He had been guarding the tree ever since, too ashamed to face her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
