{
  "bridge_text": "With the grey fox Mosk watching her from his perch, Lina stood her ground, refusing to leave while the mystery of that strange sound still pulled at her heart.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs spiraled downward into the dark. Perched on the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a worn-out green vest. This was Mosk, the guardian of the wood. His voice rasped like dry leaves as he warned Lina that the tree was no place for a girl, and she should turn back at once. He insisted she must forget the humming she heard, but Lina shook her head. She could not forget a song she had not yet truly found."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

